KNOWNBUG libstdcxx
main.cpp
--cpp11 --object-bits 12 --unwind 6 --unwinding-assertions
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ decimal: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ hex: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ showbase uppercase: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ internal padding: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] line \d+ left padding: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.6\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
unwinding assertion loop \d+: FAILURE
--
libc++ formats an integer with snprintf, whose model wrote unknown
characters, and with __num_put_base::__format_int and __identify_padding,
which had no model.  With libstdc++ the checks passed already; one stream
that is reset with str("") between the checks makes the libstdc++ run
take more than 900 s, so each check has its own stream.
